    grammarWatch:"Overuse of nominalisation creates dense, impenetrable prose. Academic writing benefits from it; plain communication does not. Know when to nominalise and when to use an active verb for clarity.",
    grammarTip:"In formal emails, reports, and presentations, nominalisation adds authority: 'We propose the implementation of a new protocol' sounds more professional than 'We propose implementing a new protocol.'",
    listeningTitle:"Who is responsible when AI decides?",
    listeningDesc:"Listen to a tech ethicist explain the challenges of AI governance.",
