    grammarWatch:"Mixed conditionals are not just grammar — they express regret, irony, and analysis of cause and effect across time. Getting them right signals C1/C2 mastery. The most common error is using 'would have' in the IF-clause: ✗ 'If I would have known…' → ✓ 'If I had known…'",
    grammarTip:"Mixed conditionals appear frequently in personal storytelling: 'If I hadn't taken that job (past), I wouldn't be where I am today (present).' Practise narrating your own turning points.",
