    grammarWatch:"In difficult conversations, cleft sentences prevent misunderstanding: 'What I said was X' (not what you heard). 'It is your tone I am reacting to, not your point.' Precision prevents escalation.",
    grammarTip:"WH-clefts open space in a dialogue: 'What concerns me is not the cost — it is the timeline.' This tells your counterpart exactly what to address, making the conversation more productive.",
