    grammarRule:"FUTURE IN THE PAST: 'was/were going to', 'would', and 'was/were about to' describe a future as it was understood from a past perspective. MIXED CONDITIONALS (review): past hypothetical + present or past result. Together, these allow analysis of how past decisions shape present realities.",
